Android ARM64 builds modify one Go 1.27.3 standard-library CPU-detection guard
through a source overlay. IdolyPride_client contributors changed this on
2026-11-10 to skip the optional MIDR/Neoverse tuning probe on Android, where
the API35 ARM translator advertises CPUID but rejects MRS MIDR_EL1.
All hardware-capability assignments and live-calculation sources are unchanged.
Original and modified Go source, the exact diff and SHA-256 pins are in
runtime-patches/go1.27.3/. This Go source remains under the Go Authors' BSD
license, preserved in third-party-licenses/Go-LICENSE. The installed Go SDK
is never modified; Linux, macOS and Android x86_64 do not use this overlay.
